---
import ReferenceTable from '../../components/ReferenceTable.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { seo } from '../../data/seo';
import snapshot from '../../../public/review/2026-10-11.1/manifest.json';
const meta = seo.review;
const files = `/review/${snapshot.reviewId}`;
const source = `${snapshot.sourceRepository}/tree/${snapshot.sourceCommit}`;
---

<DocumentLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType}>
  <ContentCard class="review-package">
<p class="section-kicker">Technical review package · {snapshot.reviewId}</p>
    <h2>Pinned source and evaluation baseline</h2>
    <p>This package contains the Core implementation candidate, its source archive, artifact manifest, reference cases, validation results, and review forms. Its technical target is fixed at source commit <a href={source}><code>{snapshot.sourceCommit}</code></a>.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/graphs/">609-question working graph</a> and <a href="/graphs/profiles/">event profiles</a> have later revisions. They are documented separately in the <a href="/graphs/coverage/">coverage ledger</a> and are not part of this earlier snapshot.</p>
    <div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href={`${files}/review-package.zip`} download>Download review package · ZIP</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="/investigation-lab/">Reference investigations</Button></div>
    <p><a href={`${files}/README.md`}>Review brief</a> · <a href={`${files}/manifest.json`}>Artifact manifest</a> · <a href={`${files}/validation.json`}>Validation baseline</a> · <a href={`${files}/walkthrough.md`}>Review walkthrough</a> · <a href={`${files}/review-form.md`}>Finding form</a></p>
    <h2>Package contents</h2>
    <ReferenceTable label="Review package contents"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Version</th><th>Scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Founding proposal</td><td>0.1.0</td><td>Purpose, 38 proposed Core requirements, and governance proposal.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Core record binding</td><td>0.1.0-draft.1</td><td>Investigation-record representation and reference implementation.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Earlier evidence-route graph</td><td>0.20261011b</td><td>103 questions, 225 edges, evidence criteria, and 252 author-side scenarios.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Published graph archive</td><td>0.20260206e</td><td>588 questions and 1,554 routes under the original graph schema.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Source archive</td><td>{snapshot.sourceCommit.slice(0,12)}</td><td>All {snapshot.files.length} tracked source files at the pinned commit.</td></tr>
    </tbody></ReferenceTable>
    <h2>Review workflow</h2>
    <ol><li><strong>Contract:</strong> compare the <a href="/founding/01-core-contract.md">Core requirements</a> with the binding and implementation behavior.</li><li><strong>Records:</strong> inspect the agent-transfer and identity cases in the <a href="/investigation-lab/">Lab</a>, including unknowns, revisions, and export/reimport.</li><li><strong>Routes:</strong> compare entry questions and yes/no/unknown branches in the snapshot with their evidence criteria.</li><li><strong>Exchange:</strong> compare separately developed readers or exporters and record preserved, unsupported, and lost meaning.</li><li><strong>Findings:</strong> cite an exact version and requirement or question ID, a minimal example, observed behavior, and untested scope.</li></ol>
    <h2>Baseline reproduction</h2>
    <p>The ZIP contains <code>source.tar.gz</code>, its manifest, and the snapshot verifier. After extraction into an empty directory, Python 3.9 or later can verify archive and source-file hashes. The Core checks use Node.js 24.21.0 and npm 11.19.0.</p>
    <pre><code>{`python3 verify-snapshot.py /absolute/path/to/extracted-source
cd /absolute/path/to/extracted-source
npm ci
npm run check
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/legacy -q
python3 scripts/validate_release_contract.py
python3 scripts/evaluate_entry_scenarios.py`}</code></pre>
    <p>The recorded baseline includes 161 Node tests, two Core cases, 58 Python tests, release preservation, and 252 route scenarios. <a href={`${files}/validation.json`}>The validation record</a> identifies the environment, checks, and limitations.</p>
    <h2>Evaluation status</h2>
    <p>Core remains an unratified candidate. The supplied cases and route reconstructions are illustrative; no original incident logs are supplied. External technical review, independent exchange, CASE/UCO mapping and loss analysis, and field evaluation remain open.</p>
    <h2>Finding process</h2>
    <p><a href="/governance/">Current stewardship</a> and the <a href="/docs/review-process.md">finding process</a> identify review handling, responses, and dissent. Public reports use fictional or authorized material. Sensitive vulnerabilities use <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/security/advisories/new">private vulnerability reporting</a>.</p>
    <div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=implementation-report.yml">Technical finding</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="/contribute/">Contribution guide</Button></div>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>

<style>
  .review-package { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .review-package pre { overflow-wrap: normal; }
</style>
